#: src/graphics-windowing.md:1
msgid "Windowing and Graphics"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:3
msgid "Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:5
msgid "VESA (vesad)"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:7
msgid ""
"vesad is not really a driver, it writes to a framebuffer given by firmware "
"(via UEFI or BIOS software interrupts)."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:9
msgid ""
"Because we don't have GPU drivers yet, we rely on what firmware gives to us."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:11
msgid "Intel GPUs"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:13
msgid "The `ihdgd` driver supports mode setting in Tiger Lake GPUs and later."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:15
msgid "GPUs"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:17
msgid ""
"On Linux/BSDs, the kernel communication with GPU is done by the Linux DRM "
"drivers (Direct Rendering Manager) and user-space applications use the "
"`libdrm` library to access them, which Mesa3D drivers use to work (Mesa3D "
"implements OpenGL/Vulkan drivers, DRM exposes the hardware interfaces)."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:19
msgid ""
"That said, in Redox a \"Linux DRM driver\" needs to be a user-space driver "
"daemon which uses the system calls/schemes to communicate with the hardware."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:21
msgid ""
"Our windowing system (Orbital) support the user-space side of Linux DRM API "
"(`libdrm` C library and Rust equivalent) to reduce user-space porting effort "
"to use our GPU driver API."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:23
msgid ""
"For software rendering we implemented a Redox backend in our Mesa3D [fork]"
"(https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/mesa)/[recipe](https://gitlab.redox-os."
"org/redox-os/cookbook/-/blob/master/recipes/mesa/recipe.toml) to use "
"LLVMPipe."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:25
msgid "Software Rendering"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:27
msgid ""
"As we don't support 2D/3D hardware acceleration yet, we use [LLVMpipe]"
"(https://docs.mesa3d.org/drivers/llvmpipe.html) to support OpenGL and Vulkan "
"applications for CPU rendering."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:29
msgid "Orbital"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:31
msgid ""
"Orbital is the default Redox desktop environment which have a display "
"server, window manager, wallpaper daemon, effects compositor, image viewer "
"and basic terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:33
msgid ""
"It was prefered over Wayland and X11 to avoid their requirements, "
"dependencies, and limitations (EGL on Wayland and GLX on X11). Orbital was "
"much more simple ans easier for the immature Redox API and had the fastest "
"native software rendering performance."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:35
msgid "Comparison with X11/Wayland"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:37
msgid ""
"This display server is more simple than X11 and Wayland making the porting "
"task more quick and easy, it's not advanced like X11 and Wayland yet but "
"enough to port most Linux/BSD programs."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:39
msgid ""
"Compared to Wayland, Orbital has one protocol server implementation (like "
"X11 for a long time), while Wayland provides protocols for compositors and "
"clients."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:41
msgid ""
"Also native software rendering on X11 and Wayland applications is rare, "
"which would reduce Redox performance by partially or fully using LLVMPipe on "
"applications or user session."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:43
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:45
msgid "Custom Resolutions"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:46
msgid "App Launcher (bottom bar)"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:47
msgid "File Manager"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:48
msgid "Text Editor"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:49
msgid "Calculator"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:50
msgid "Terminal Emulator"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:52
msgid ""
"If you hold the **Super** key (generally the key with a Windows logo) it "
"will show all keyboard shortcuts in a pop-up."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:54
msgid "Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:56
msgid "Programs using the following libraries can work on Orbital."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:58
msgid "winit"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:59
msgid "softbuffer"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:60
msgid "Slint (through winit and softbuffer)"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:61
msgid "Iced (through winit and softbuffer)"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:62
msgid "egui (winit or SDL2 can be used)"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:63
msgid "SDL1.2"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:64
msgid "SDL2"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:65
msgid "Mesa3D's OSMesa"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:67
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:69
msgid ""
"In Orbital a GUI program cannot read input events or the content "
"(framebuffer) from windows of other GUI programs, like Wayland."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:71
msgid "Clients"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:73
msgid ""
"Apps (or 'clients') create a window and draw to it by using the [orbclient]"
"(https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/orbclient) client."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:76
msgid "Client Examples"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:78
msgid ""
"If you wish to see examples of client apps that use [orbclient](https://"
"gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/orbclient) to \"talk\" to Orbital and create "
"windows and draw to them, then you can find some in [orbclient/examples]"
"(https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/orbclient/-/tree/master/examples) "
"folder."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:82
msgid "Porting"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:84
msgid "If you want to port a program to Orbital, see below:"
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:86
msgid ""
"If the program is written in Rust it probably works on Orbital because the "
"`winit` crate is used in most places, but there are programs that access X11 "
"or Wayland directly. You need to port these programs to `winit` and merge to "
"upstream."
msgstr ""

#: src/graphics-windowing.md:88
msgid ""
"If the program is written in C or C++ and accesses X11 or Wayland directly, "
"it must be ported to the [Orbital library](https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-"
"os/liborbital)."
msgstr ""
